{"route": [54, 74, 53, 65], "explanation": "A flat, compact food route along the T1 tram line, which is wheelchair-accessible, avoiding places with stairs or steep hills such as Pandeli, Vefa Bozacısı and Van Kahvaltı Evi. Start with lunch at Tarihi Sultanahmet Köftecisi, serving the same meatballs since 1920 in a simple, easy-to-enter setting. Then head down to the flat Eminönü shore for balık ekmek (grilled mackerel sandwiches) from the boats, Istanbul's classic street food; you can eat from your wheelchair by the water instead of on the low stools. Next door, Hamdi Restoran has an elevator up to its Golden Horn terrace for pistachio kebab and lahmacun. Finish by crossing the flat Galata Bridge to Karaköy Güllüoğlu for Istanbul's most famous pistachio baklava. Avoid weekends and peak hours in Eminönü, when crowds make moving around harder."}
